      "writtenOn": "2024-12-03T15:38:53Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I think you might run into some trouble with the alignment of the base address now that you are using masking behind the scenes. The architectures requires that:\n\n```\nIf DBGWCR\u003cn\u003e_EL1.MASK is nonzero, and any masked bits of DBGWVR\u003cn\u003e_EL1 are\nnot 0, it is CONSTRAINED UNPREDICTABLE whether the watchpoint generates a Watchpoint exception when the unmasked bits match.\n```\n\nSo you will need to make sure that the base address is naturally aligned to the size of the watchpoint region. I don\u0027t see anything in your userspace code to ensure that (e.g. `MapData()` just calls `mmap()` without a fixes address).",
      "range": {
